  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 230 PM MST WED NOV 18 2026\nA brief upper-level ridge will build into the region Saturday, \nbringing dry conditions. Behind it, a strong upper-level low \npressure system will weaken as it moves onshore into the Pacific NW, \nbringing precipitation chances to the area starting Saturday night \ninto Sunday morning. Precipitation chances will be 30-60% for higher \nelevations and 10-20% for lower elevations through Monday afternoon.\nAnother brief upper-level ridge will sweep across the area late \nMonday into early Tuesday before another Pacific system moves in and \nbrings widespread precipitation chances yet again for Wednesday.\nWith these systems moving through, higher elevation precipitation \ntype will be snow, while lower elevations will be more uncertain \nthis far out. Timing of the precipitation will be important, along \nwith any cold pools that remain in lower valleys. The forecast \ncurrently reflects this uncertainty, with a wintry mix being the \npredominant precipitation type. Temperatures will hover near or \nslightly below normal in SW Idaho and 5-10 degrees below normal in \nSE Oregon throughout the long term period.",
